er, if any descendant is already selected, skip it. So we need to efficiently know descendants for each cluster. We can precompute descendant lists for each retained cluster.\n\n- Return all retained clusters with stability, and selected_cluster_ids sorted ascending.\n\nEdge cases: no clusters retained? Then clusters array empty, selected empty.\n\nImplementation details in Python: standard library only, no imports beyond json maybe (but solve returns dict, no need to serialize). We'll use list, dict, set, etc.\n\nWe need to output the code as a JSON string under \"implementation\". So we'll write the Python source code as a string, properly escaped for JSON. Then embed it in a JSON object with key \"implementation\". The entire response must be exactly that JSON object.\n\nLet's write the solve function.\n\nPseudo:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # extract fields\n    min_size = case['min_cluster_size']\n    clusters_raw = case['clusters']\n    parent_map_raw = case['parent']\n    \n    # Validate? Assume valid per contract.\n    # Build dict of cluster objects keyed by id\n    clusters_dict = {c['cluster_id']: c for c in clusters_raw}\n    \n    # Filter retained clusters (size >= min_size)\n    retained = {cid: c for cid, c in clusters_dict.items() if c['size'] >= min_size}\n    \n    # Compute stability for each retained cluster\n    stabilities = {}\n    for cid, c in retained.items():\n        total = 0.0\n        birth = c['birth_lambda']\n        for exit_lambda in c['point_exit_lambdas']:\n            total += max(0.0, exit_lambda - birth)\n        stabilities[cid] = total\n    \n    # Build parent relationships among retained clusters\n    # parent_map_raw maps cid to parent or None\n    # For each retained cid, find parent if retained, else None\n    retained_parent = {}\n    for cid in retained:\n        par = parent_map_raw.get(cid)  # None if not present? but it's in payload\n        if par is not None and par in retained:\n            retained_parent[cid] = par\n        else:\n            retained_parent[cid] = None\n    \n    # Build children lists\n    children = {cid: [] for cid in retained}\n    for cid, par in retained_parent.items():\n        if par is not None:\n            children[par].append(cid)\n    \n    # Precompute descendants for each cluster\n    # We'll compute using DFS recursion (stack safe due to limited size)\n    descendants = {}\n    def get_descendants(cid):\n        if cid in descendants:\n            return descendants[cid]\n        desc = set()\n        for child in children[cid]:\n            desc.add(child)\n            desc.update(get_descendants(child))\n        descendants[cid] = desc\n        return desc\n    \n    for cid in retained:\n        get_descendants(cid)\n    \n    # Sort retained clusters: descending stability, then ascending cluster_id\n    sorted_clusters = sorted(retained.keys(), key=lambda cid: (-stabilities[cid], cid))\n    \n    selected = []\n    blocked = set()  # ancestors that are blocked (cannot be selected)\n    selected_set = set()\n    \n    for cid in sorted_clusters:\n        if cid in blocked:\n            continue\n        # Check if any descendant is already selected\n        desc = descendants[cid]\n        if selected_set & desc:\n            continue\n        # Select this cluster\n        selected.append(cid)\n        selected_set.add(cid)\n        # Block ancestors\n        # Walk up parent chain\n        current = cid\n        while current is not None:\n            current = retained_parent.get(current)\n            if current is not None:\n                blocked.add(current)\n            else:\n                break\n    \n    # Build output clusters array\n    out_clusters = []\n    for cid in sorted(retained.keys()):  # maybe sort by cluster_id? Not specified, but typical to keep order? Output schema just array. Let's sort by cluster_id for consistency.\n        c = retained[cid]\n        out_clusters.append({\n            \"cluster_id\": cid,\